      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "My hands sweat, it's a very annoying issue in VRChat as I can't adjust my release grip value. The Index controllers can be squeezed to 125% force. If you set your grip to 110% and release to 99%, this eliminated sticking hands due to sweat. This feature is available in the Zenith MMO and works great. It would help so much in VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-11T02:52:48.568Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The Index Controllers have this squeeze grip that can read the amount of force applied to it. VRChat is not making use of this. If you do the fist gesture, unlike on for instance the Oculus, the input on the Index right now is binary. I want to have the same kind of progressive control on my Index Controllers as I did with the Oculus Touch. I propose having VRChat toggle the fist gesture once all fingers are laid down and the grip is being squeezed, having a small value range so we don't have to squeeze the grip too hard in order for us to have like our eyes fully closed yet still have that amount of control where we an partially close our eyes.",
